items/lem-null-times-bounded.md:62:[L4] Order arithmetic in $\mathbb{R}$: $0 < 1$, adding a constant preserves the strict order, and $\le$ and $<$ compose transitively ([[cor-of-one-positive]], [[lem-of-add-order]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
items/lem-null-times-bounded.md:64:[L5] Inverses: if $c > 0$ then $c^{-1} > 0$, so $\varepsilon/c > 0$ whenever $\varepsilon > 0$ and $c > 0$ ([[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[lem-of-sign-rules]]).
items/lem-null-times-bounded.md:66:[L6] Real versus rational $\varepsilon$: for every real $\eta > 0$ there is a rational $\varepsilon$ with $0 < \varepsilon < \eta$, by density ([[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]) or by the Archimedean property ([[thm-of-archimedean]]) applied to $1/\eta$; consequently the convergence test of [[def-real-limit]] may equivalently be run with real $\varepsilon > 0$ ([[def-sequence]]).
items/lem-convergent-implies-bounded.md:52:[L1] Convergence: for every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K \in \mathbb{N}$ with $|x_k - x| < \varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$ ([[def-real-limit]]); and $1$ is a rational $> 0$, since $\mathbb{Q}$ is an ordered field ([[thm-rat-ordered-field]]) and $0 < 1$ in every ordered field ([[cor-of-one-positive]]).
items/lem-convergent-implies-bounded.md:54:[L2] Triangle inequality: $|a + b| \le |a| + |b|$ in $\mathbb{R}$ ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
items/lem-convergent-implies-bounded.md:56:[L3] Absolute value: $|u| \ge 0$ for every real $u$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
items/lem-convergent-implies-bounded.md:58:[L4] Finite maxima: for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and all reals $a_0, \dots, a_n$ the set $\{a_0, \dots, a_n\}$ has a maximum ([[lem-finite-set-has-max]]); a maximum lies in the set and dominates every element of it ([[def-max-min]]).
items/lem-convergent-implies-bounded.md:60:[L5] Order arithmetic in $\mathbb{R}$: transitivity of $\le$ and of $<$; both mixed forms, $u < v \le w \Rightarrow u < w$ and $u \le v < w \Rightarrow u < w$, and the implication $u < v \Rightarrow u \le v$, all immediate from the reading of $u \le v$ as "$u < v$ or $u = v$" ([[def-complete-ordered-field]], [[def-ordered-field]]); and translation invariance, $a < b \Rightarrow a + c < b + c$ ([[lem-of-add-order]]).
items/lem-convergent-implies-bounded.md:62:[L6] The order on $\mathbb{N}$ is total, so every index $k$ satisfies $k < K$ or $k \ge K$ ([[thm-nat-linear-order]]).
