FILE items/lem-of-abs-value.md
34:## Statement
35:
36:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) and let $x, y \in F$, with
37:$|x|$ the absolute value ([[def-abs-value]]). Then
38:
39:$$|x| \ge 0; \quad |x| = 0 \iff x = 0; \quad -|x| \le x \le |x|; \quad |-x| = |x|; \quad |xy| = |x|\,|y|;$$
40:
41:and, for every $c > 0$, one has $|x| < c \iff -c < x < c$.
42:
43:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/lem-of-add-order.md
33:## Statement
34:
35:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) with positive cone $P$, and
36:let $a, b, c, d \in F$.
37:
38:1. **Translation invariance.** If $a < b$ then $a + c < b + c$.
39:2. **Adding inequalities.** If $a < b$ and $c < d$ then $a + c < b + d$.
40:
41:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/lem-of-inverse-positive.md
33:## Statement
34:
35:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) with positive cone $P$, and
36:let $a, b \in F$.
37:
38:1. If $a > 0$ then $a^{-1} > 0$.
39:2. If $0 < a < b$ then $0 < b^{-1} < a^{-1}$.
40:
41:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/lem-of-sign-rules.md
33:## Statement
34:
35:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) with positive cone $P$, and
36:let $a, b, c \in F$.
37:
38:1. If $a > 0$ and $b > 0$ then $ab > 0$.
39:2. If $a > 0$ and $b < 0$ then $ab < 0$.
40:3. If $a < 0$ and $b < 0$ then $ab > 0$.
41:4. If $c > 0$ then $a < b \iff ac < bc$.
42:5. If $c < 0$ then $a < b \iff bc < ac$ (multiplication by a negative reverses order).
43:
44:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/lem-of-triangle-inequality.md
34:## Statement
35:
36:Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) and let $x, y \in F$. Then
37:
38:$$|x + y| \le |x| + |y|.$$
39:
40:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/lem-rat-embeds-dense.md
31:## Statement
32:
33:The map $q \mapsto \hat q$ ([[def-real-numbers]]) is an embedding of ordered
34:fields. Every real is approximated by rationals: for $x \in \mathbb{R}$ and
35:rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $q \in \mathbb{Q}$ with
36:$|x - \hat q| < \hat\varepsilon$. Consequently, strictly between any two
37:reals lies a rational.
38:
39:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/prop-of-multiply-inequalities.md
33:## Statement
34:
35:Let $F$ be an ordered field. If $0 < a < b$ and $0 < c < d$ then $ac < bd$. If $0 \le a \le b$ and $0 \le c \le d$ then $ac \le bd$.
36:
37:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/thm-nat-linear-order.md
35:## Statement
36:
37:The relation $\le$ on $\mathbb{N}$, where $m \le n \iff \exists k\ (m + k = n)$ ([[def-nat-order]]), is a linear (total) order: reflexive, antisymmetric, transitive, and total.
38:
39:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/thm-of-archimedean.md
34:## Statement
35:
36:Every complete ordered field $F$ ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]) is Archimedean:
37:for every $x \in F$ there is a natural number $n \ge 1$ with $x < n \cdot 1_F$,
38:where $n \cdot 1_F$ is the canonical natural of the ordered field $F$
39:([[def-ordered-field]]). Equivalently, the canonical naturals are cofinal in $F$.
40:
41:## Facts & Assumptions
FILE items/thm-rat-ordered-field.md
33:## Statement
34:
35:The relation of [[def-rat-order]] is well defined and makes the field
36:$\mathbb{Q}$ ([[thm-rat-field]]) a totally ordered field: the order is total,
37:$x \le y$ implies $x + z \le y + z$, and $0 < x$, $0 < y$ imply
38:$0 < xy$.
39:
40:## Facts & Assumptions

