    71	
    72	3.1 For all $k, l \ge K$ we get $|x_k - x_l| = |(x_k - x) + (x - x_l)| \le |x_k - x| + |x - x_l| = |x_k - x| + |x_l - x|$, while adding the two strict inequalities of step 2.1 gives $|x_k - x| + |x_l - x| < \varepsilon/2 + \varepsilon/2 = \varepsilon$; composing the non-strict inequality with the strict one yields $|x_k - x_l| < \varepsilon$. [step 2.1, L2, L3, L4, L5, L6]
